            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="0365" n="271" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg271"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.01/213: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-04-14T19:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 14,
                                1924—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 14—5:15
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>62. Legation’s 57, March 25, 10 p.m. General surprise at plebiscite return
                    indicating as many as 65 to 70 percent of voters favor republic.</p>
                <p>Royalists will probably develop into bitter and increasingly strong political
                    party not advocating return to monarchy but opposing radical democrats.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
